    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p>Bug Type: Functional / Collision<br/>
Priority: Medium</p>

<p>Preconditions:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Game is running.</li>
	<li>Doraemon is selected and the player is in gameplay.</li>
	<li>A wooden crate is present in the room.</li>
</ul>


<p>Steps to Reproduce:</p>

<ol>
	<li>Select Doraemon on the Character Select screen and start the game.</li>
	<li>Move to a position where a wooden crate is between Doraemon and an enemy (or an empty space behind the crate).</li>
	<li>Aim at the crate with the mouse.</li>
	<li>Press the left mouse button to use the basic attack.</li>
	<li>Observe how the attack interacts with the crate.</li>
</ol>


<p>Expected Result:</p>

<ul>
	<li>The basic attack is blocked by the wooden crate and disappears on contact, the same as for walls and stone pillars (TC-MI-05).</li>
	<li>The attack does not reach targets behind the crate.</li>
</ul>


<p>Actual Result:</p>

<ul>
	<li>The basic attack passes through the wooden crate and keeps flying.</li>
	<li><span class="error">&#91;Nếu có&#93;</span> It can hit enemies behind the crate.</li>
</ul>


<p>Test Case Result:</p>

<ul>
	<li>FAIL</li>
	<li>Related Test Cases: TC-MI-05 (projectile disappears on hitting a wall), TC-MP-08 (wooden crate decoration), TC-MV-05 (collision with walls and pillars)</li>
	<li>No dedicated test case exists for Doraemon yet.</li>
</ul>


<p>Notes:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Likely the crate’s collision layer or mask is not included in Doraemon’s attack collision.</li>
	<li>Check whether other characters’ attacks (Miya’s arrows, Charlotte, Pyrois) are blocked by crates and whether stone pillars block Doraemon’s attack.</li>
	<li>This may allow players to attack safely through obstacles, so check how it affects enemies in the room.</li>
	<li>Attach a screen recording.</li>
</ul>

            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
